1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,592
Earth stops for one second.

2
00:00:01,612 --> 00:00:02,656
You don't.

3
00:00:02,676 --> 00:00:04,159
Neither does the air.

4
00:00:04,179 --> 00:00:05,642
Or the oceans.

5
00:00:05,662 --> 00:00:08,154
Or that sandwich you were holding.

6
00:00:08,174 --> 00:00:09,294
Half a heartbeat later,

7
00:00:09,294 --> 00:00:11,917
you're hurtling east at about Mach 1.4.

8
00:00:11,937 --> 00:00:13,086
That's faster than the speed

9
00:00:13,086 --> 00:00:13,773
of sound.

10
00:00:13,793 --> 00:00:14,793
In that one second,

11
00:00:14,813 --> 00:00:17,503
you'd cover 465 meters:

12
00:00:17,523 --> 00:00:18,548
about four and a half

13
00:00:18,548 --> 00:00:19,231
football pitches.

14
00:00:20,581 --> 00:00:21,561
The good news:

15
00:00:21,581 --> 00:00:22,742
you won't fly for long.

16
00:00:22,762 --> 00:00:23,754
Gravity pulls you to the

17
00:00:23,754 --> 00:00:25,366
ground in about half a second.

18
00:00:25,386 --> 00:00:26,466
The bad news:

19
00:00:26,486 --> 00:00:28,090
you land moving almost twice

20
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:29,807
as fast as a cruising jet.

21
00:00:29,827 --> 00:00:31,185
Sideways.

22
00:00:31,205 --> 00:00:32,987
Into everything that just stopped.

23
00:00:33,007 --> 00:00:33,921
Which is...

24
00:00:33,941 --> 00:00:35,474
everything.

25
00:00:35,494 --> 00:00:36,941
Subscribe for more what ifs!
